desktop-shell: windows too big for their screen are maximized on it

A window bigger than the work area of its screen is asked to fit it
(patches 0005 and 0009), but some apps ignore the size they are given, or
cannot get that small (their minimum size is bigger than the screen, e.g.
on a small or zoomed screen). Such a window stayed at the top left of the
screen, partly off it and under the taskbar.

- If a window asked to fit its screen is still too big a second later,
  it is maximized on that screen, which makes it exactly as big as the
  work area. Fixed-size windows (minimum size = maximum size) are left
  alone. Weston logs each case ("hexaOS: window ... maximizing it").
- A window restored from maximized or full screen (not by dragging it)
  may come back at a size it remembered from a bigger screen: it is now
  kept inside its screen, as a new window is.

